# Agent runtime

Each specialist is a `SpecialistDef`: `id`, `keywords`, `tools`, `system`, `demo()`.

- Register new agents in `registry.ts` and add the id to `AgentId`.
- Tools are local, deterministic functions in `tools.ts`. Do not call the network from tools unless the user asked for a live integration.
- The orchestrator must keep emitting `AgentEvent` in order: plan, start, tool, end, token, done.
- `demo()` must still produce a usable founder memo when no API key is set.
- Planner picks 2–4 specialists. Always keep strategy unless the ask is purely ops.

```ts
export const exampleAgent: SpecialistDef = {
  id: "example",
  name: "Example",
  title: "One-line job",
  blurb: "When this agent should run.",
  accent: "#c4622d",
  keywords: ["example"],
  tools: [],
  system: "You are Foundry's Example agent for SMEs. Be concrete.",
  demo: ({ context }) => ({
    summary: `Do the next useful thing for ${context.name}.`,
    bullets: ["One action this week."],
  }),
};
```
